# Range-Based Resolver Test Patterns

## Intersection Coverage Scenarios

### RangeBasedBreakRuleTimeRangeResolver Intersection Branches
The `intersection.isEmpty()` branch in [RangeBasedBreakRuleTimeRangeResolver.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/rules/timerange_resolver/range_based/RangeBasedBreakRuleTimeRangeResolver.java) must be covered:

```java
if (!intersection.isEmpty()) {
    constrainedRanges.add(intersection);
}
```

### Required Test Scenarios

#### 1. Empty Intersection Test
```java
@Test
void testResolveTimeRangeWithBreakIntervalAdjacentToWorkPeriod() {
    // Given
    given(this.timeLog.getWorkStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(9, 0));
    given(this.timeLog.getWorkEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(17, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(17, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(18, 0));
    
    // When
    RangeSet<LocalTime> result = this.resolver.resolveTimeRange(this.context);
    
    // Then
    assertThat(result).isNotNull();
    assertThat(result.isEmpty()).isTrue();
    // intersection.isEmpty() returns true, so nothing is added
}
```

#### 2. Non-Empty Intersection Test
```java
@Test
void testResolveTimeRangeWithBreakIntervalPartiallyOverlappingWorkPeriod() {
    // Given
    given(this.timeLog.getWorkStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(9, 0));
    given(this.timeLog.getWorkEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(17, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(8, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(13, 0));
    
    // When
    RangeSet<LocalTime> result = this.resolver.resolveTimeRange(this.context);
    
    // Then
    assertThat(result).isNotNull();
    assertThat(result.isEmpty()).isFalse();
    // intersection.isEmpty() returns false, so intersection is added
}
```

## Range-Based Test Patterns

### Test Setup for Range-Based Resolvers
```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class RangeBasedResolverTests {
    @Mock private Logger logger;
    @Mock private TimeLog timeLog;
    @Mock private TimeLogBreakInterval breakInterval1;
    @Mock private TimeRangeResolverContext context;
    
    private RangeBasedResolver resolver;
    
    @BeforeEach
    void setUp() {
        this.resolver = new RangeBasedResolver(this.logger);
    }
}
```

### Break Interval Validation Tests
```java
@Test
void testResolveTimeRangeWithInvalidBreakInterval() {
    // Given
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(13, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(12, 0)); // Invalid
    
    // When
    RangeSet<LocalTime> result = this.resolver.resolveTimeRange(this.context);
    
    // Then
    assertThat(result).isNotNull();
    assertThat(result.isEmpty()).isTrue();
}
```

### Work Period Constraint Tests
```java
@Test
void testResolveTimeRangeWithBreakIntervalOutsideWorkPeriod() {
    // Given
    given(this.timeLog.getWorkStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(9, 0));
    given(this.timeLog.getWorkEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(17, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakStartTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(18, 0));
    given(this.breakInterval1.getBreakEndTime()).willReturn(LocalTime.of(19, 0));
    
    // When
